  "body": "## Summary\n\nDepends on #396. This is the accounting prerequisite for held-refund recovery,\nnot a claim that the PayPal GET adapter or admin resolution command is finished.\n\n- Reproduce and repair verified refunds leaving canonical intents captured with zero refunded money/history.\n- Lock and validate original checkout/attempt/intent evidence and aggregate totals, then advance the canonical state machine in the same transaction as refund, checkout, ledger, credit-note record and audit.\n- Refuse historical drift/disputes instead of silently rewriting them; preserve the execution fence, immutable refs and exact completion replay.\n- Fix a distinct Int64-overflow bug in the canonical refund transition; add deterministic and generated whole-range checks.\n- Document rollout, rollback, exact commands, source-backed next recovery boundary and remaining work. Regenerate catalog reports without adding an exception.\n\n## Dependencies and review order\n\nExisting core/provider stack \u2192 #393 \u2192 #396 \u2192 this PR. Base is\n`codex/payment-refund-execution-safety-20260916`.\nLatest observed main `7eafd3f479817f267ba0de6592c3e16ea920f4ae` was merged locally;\nit introduced no file changes because the secret-example cleanup was already inherited.\nNo GitHub PR was merged. Newer #331 and mobile #83 changes were inspected but need\na separate safe integration preserving mobile #82 query/evidence history.\n\n## Verified tests\n\n- Red canonical money test: 4 examples / 1 expected failure (actual overflow).\n- Red real PostgreSQL suite: 231 examples / 6 expected failures (intent drift and validation gaps).\n- Fixed fresh PostgreSQL migration/runtime suite: **231 / 0**, including concurrent partial refunds, exact replay, drift/dispute rejection and whole-transaction rollback.\n- Final full Stack suite: **2632 / 0**, resolver lts-24.42 / GHC 9.10.3. Runtime frozen at `0d8dc52655f1eb5b485cae500f476ed5188a2a7d`; final test source `6723bd8436e33d36c604cfba376a2d90f912436e` adds only a pure money property.\n- Repository quality: **232 / 0**; no critical/error formal findings, advisory warnings retained.\n- Catalog gate: **1433 files / 1135 reviewed candidates**, unchanged decisions.\n- Diff whitespace, local documentation links, unchanged OpenAPI/web/mobile diffs and generated web/mobile byte comparison passed.\n\nExact timestamps, commands, logs and limits: `docs/payments/refund-accounting-2026-09-16.md`.\nNo UI/native/device/screenshot/sandbox/staging test or live provider transaction was performed.\nParent #396 backend and UI CI succeeded; those are not CI results for this PR.\nBoth disposable synthetic PostgreSQL clusters are stopped; data/logs retained.\n\n## Compatibility, migration, configuration and risks\n\nNo migration/backfill, API/DTO/client/UI change, secret change or provider activation.\nKeep refund execution disabled until merchant/sandbox and recovery qualification.\nDrain older writers before rollout. Before binary rollback, disable affected refund\ncommands and preserve all financial evidence: an older binary can recreate drift.\n\nAlready-succeeded history is not rewritten on replay. Null intent links remain\nnull (retained by code inspection; new refund fixtures use canonical links).\nDisputed or inconsistent aggregates intentionally remain held. This may require\noperator review even after the provider returned a successful refund. Never issue\na second POST, cancel the hold or alter balances just to make reconciliation pass.\n\nUnfinished: provider GET recovery/admin action; unknown-ID and historical-failed\nresolution; reviewed canonical backfill; refund/dispute coordination; complete\nseller/tax/fee allocation and SRI issuance; latest upstream integration.\nExternally unverified: credentials/accounts, hosting authentication/deployed SHA,\nmerchant sandboxes, staging qualification and legal/accounting activation approval.\n",
